WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.870
Harvest time in a UK wheat field.

2
00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:05.790
A combine harvester works along the rows.

3
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:12.820
In 2025, UK farmers harvested 12 million
tonnes of wheat from 1.7 million hectares.

4
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:20.450
FAO figures for 2024: UK wheat
yielded 7.28 tonnes per hectare.

5
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.310
The world average was 3.64.

6
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.170
Half the UK figure.

7
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:28.050
So what makes one field
out-produce another?

8
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.310
In this mission, you'll
model a farm as a system,

9
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.470
from inputs to outputs.

10
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.510
Then you'll measure
productivity for yourself,

11
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.710
in tonnes per hectare.

12
00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:42.110
Your mission: find out what makes
one wheat field out-produce another.
